---
import Service from '../../layouts/Service.astro';
import { serviceArea, business } from '../../data/business';
import twoFan from '../../assets/photos/blower-door-two-fan-setup.jpg';
---
<Service
  slug="commercial-blower-door-testing"
  title="Commercial Blower Door Testing | Bell Energy Solutions"
  description="Third-party commercial blower door testing, including multi-fan setups, by a Retrotec-certified tester in Eastern Washington and North Idaho."
  heading="Commercial Blower Door Testing"
  lead="Third-party air leakage testing of commercial buildings, including multi-fan setups, by a Retrotec-certified tester."
  photo="Multi-fan blower door setup on a commercial building"
  image={twoFan}
  alt="Two Retrotec blower door fans running together in one doorway"
  position="50% 62%"
>
  <h2>Whole-building air leakage testing</h2>
  <p>Commercial blower door testing measures how much air a building's envelope leaks. Fans are sealed into exterior openings and used to pressurize or depressurize the building to a set pressure difference. The airflow needed to hold that pressure shows how tight the envelope is.</p>

  <h2>Multi-fan setups</h2>
  <p>Large buildings need more airflow than a single fan can deliver. A multi-fan setup runs several blower door fans together, controlled as one system, to reach the target test pressure on bigger envelopes.</p>

  <h2>Results</h2>
  <p>Commercial results are commonly reported as airflow normalized to the building envelope area at a stated test pressure, so buildings of different sizes can be compared.</p>

  <h2>Who it's for</h2>
  <p>Builders, architects, and engineering firms working on commercial projects.</p>

  <dl class="spec" slot="aside" style="margin-top:20px">
    <div><dt>Certification</dt><dd>Retrotec certified for residential and commercial blower door testing</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Setups</dt><dd>Including multi-fan setups</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Area</dt><dd>{serviceArea.line}</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Pricing</dt><dd>{business.quoteLine}</dd></div>
  </dl>
</Service>
